  "response": {
    "text": "Expo lists `@stripe/stripe-react-native` as supported for native iOS and Android payment flows; install the Expo-compatible version with `npx expo install`. Its Google Pay and Apple Pay features require a development build and are not supported in Expo Go. Redirect-based checkout also needs a URL scheme configured in Stripe initialization. ([docs.expo.dev](https://docs.expo.dev/versions/latest/sdk/stripe/?utm_source=openai))\n\nFor digital goods or features consumed in the app, Expo’s IAP guide lists `react-native-purchases` and `expo-iap`; these use native code and require a development build rather than Expo Go. ([docs.expo.dev](https://docs.expo.dev/guides/in-app-purchases/?utm_source=openai))\n\nApple’s guidelines say physical goods or services consumed outside the app should be paid for using methods other than in-app purchase, such as Apple Pay or card entry. Digital-purchase payment options can vary by storefront and applicable entitlements. ([developer.apple.com](https://developer.apple.com/app-store/review/guidelines/?utm_source=openai))",
